EXAM_DATA.papers["1998"] = {"id":"1998","year":1998,"label":"1998 旧卷","era":"old","sourceUrl":"https://english-exam.lazynote.cn/kaoyan/paper/1998/","timeLimitMin":180,"scoreMode":"raw","parts":[{"id":"section1","kind":"cloze","title":"Section I 完形填空","directions":"Directions: For each numbered blank in the following passage,there are four choices marked [A].[B].[C].and [D].Choose the best one and mark your answer on ANSWER SHEET 1 by blackening the corresponding letter in the brackets with a pencil.(10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section1-1","text":"Until recently most historians spoke very critically of the Industrial Revolution. They   {{1}}   that in the long run industrialization greatly raised the standard of living for the   {{2}}   man. But they insisted that its   {{3}}   results during the period from 1750 to 1850 were widespread poverty and misery for the   {{4}}   of the English population.   {{5}}   contrast, they saw in the preceding hundred years from 1650 to 1750, when England was still a   {{6}}   agricultural country, a period of great abundance and prosperity."},{"id":"p-section1-2","text":"This view,   {{7}}   , is generally thought to be wrong. Specialists   {{8}}   history and economics have   {{9}}   two things: that the period from 1650 to 1750 was   {{10}}   by great poverty, and that industrialization certainly did not worsen and may have actually improved the conditions for the majority of the populace."}]},"questions":[{"n":1,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"admitted"},{"key":"B","text":"believed"},{"key":"C","text":"claimed"},{"key":"D","text":"predicted"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"1.","reason":"前后两句构成『让步—转折』 本句 They __(1)__ that in the long run industrialization greatly raised the standard of living 说的是好处，下一句却 But they insisted that its __(3)__ results ... were widespread poverty and misery。一个 But 把两句对立起来：第 1 空这句是史学家『承认』的让步，第 2 句才是他们真正坚持的。线索指向一个带让步色彩的动词。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"admit 是『（不情愿地）承认』，正好对上后句 But they insisted 的让步—转折结构：先承认长远好处，再坚持短期苦难。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"believe 只是『相信、认为』，平铺直叙，体现不出与后句 But they insisted 的对立让步关系，语气偏弱。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"claim 常带『（无确据地）声称』的怀疑色彩，但此处是史学家公认的事实（工业化确实抬高了生活水平），用 claim 色彩冲突。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"predict 是『预测（未来）』，而 in the long run industrialization greatly raised the standard of living 用一般过去时陈述已发生的事实，不是预测。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":2,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"plain"},{"key":"B","text":"average"},{"key":"C","text":"mean"},{"key":"D","text":"normal"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"2.","reason":"搭配对象是 man，指『普通人』 greatly raised the standard of living for the __(2)__ man 说的是工业化抬高了谁的生活水平——语境要的是『普通老百姓』。英语里『普通人/常人』的惯用说法是 the average man。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"plain man 偏向『相貌平平/直率的人』，不是统计意义上的『普通大众』，与『生活水平』语境不贴。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"the average man 是固定说法，意为『普通人、寻常百姓』，正好对上『工业化抬高了普通人生活水平』的语义。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"mean 作形容词意为『小气的、刻薄的』，色彩为贬义，与中性的『普通人』完全不符。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"normal 强调『正常的、不反常的』，英语中不用 the normal man 表『普通人』，搭配不地道。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":3,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"momentary"},{"key":"B","text":"prompt"},{"key":"C","text":"instant"},{"key":"D","text":"immediate"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"3.","reason":"与上句 in the long run 反义对照 上句说 in the long run industrialization greatly raised the standard of living（长远看是好的），本句 But ... its __(3)__ results during the period from 1750 to 1850 were widespread poverty 转而说短期内是坏的。第 3 空要的是与 in the long run（长远）相对的『直接的、近期的』之意。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"momentary 强调『一瞬即逝』，而 1750-1850 是长达百年的后果，不是瞬时的，时长不符。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"prompt 多指『（人或反应）迅速及时的』，如 prompt reply，修饰 results 表『直接后果』不地道。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"instant 指『立刻、即刻』，常用于 instant coffee 这类瞬间发生之事，与延续百年的后果矛盾。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"immediate 除『立刻』外有『直接的、眼前的』之义，immediate results 正与上句 in the long run 形成『近期 vs 长远』对照，最贴切。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":4,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"bulk"},{"key":"B","text":"host"},{"key":"C","text":"gross"},{"key":"D","text":"magnitude"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"4.","reason":"框架是 the __ of the population widespread poverty and misery for the __(4)__ of the English population，要表达的是『英国人口的大多数』。固定搭配 the bulk of=『大部分、大多数』。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"the bulk of the population 是固定说法，意为『绝大部分人口』，与『普遍贫困波及多数人』完全契合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"host 表『大量』时用 a host of（许多），不用 the ___ of the population 这个『其中大部分』的框架，搭配错。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"gross 常作形容词（gross income 总收入），此处需要名词；即便作名词也不与 of population 搭配表『大多数人』。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"magnitude 指『巨大、量级、重要程度』，不指『人口中的多数』，语义跑偏。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":5,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"On"},{"key":"B","text":"With"},{"key":"C","text":"For"},{"key":"D","text":"By"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"5.","reason":"空后是 contrast 一词 __(5)__ contrast, they saw in the preceding hundred years ... a period of great abundance，句首要表『相比之下、与此相对』，固定短语为 By contrast。这是搭配，依据就在空后那个词。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"on 配的是 on the contrary（恰恰相反），不与裸 contrast 搭配，且含义偏『正相反』而非『相比之下』。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"英语里没有 with contrast 作句首过渡语的用法，搭配不成立。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"for contrast 不是表『相比之下』的固定过渡短语，搭配错误。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"By contrast 是固定短语，意为『相比之下、与此形成对照』，正好引出前一百年与工业革命期的对比，最契合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":6,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"broadly"},{"key":"B","text":"thoroughly"},{"key":"C","text":"generally"},{"key":"D","text":"completely"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"6.","reason":"强调当时『纯』农业国 when England was still a __(6)__ agricultural country，与下文工业化形成对照，此处要凸显工业革命前英国是『完完全全的农业国』，需要表『彻底、完全』的强程度副词。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"broadly 表『大致、宽泛地』，留有余地，削弱了『纯农业国』的对照力度。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"thoroughly 强调『彻底地（做某事）』，常修饰动作（thoroughly cleaned），修饰 agricultural 这一国家属性不如 completely 自然。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"generally 表『一般、通常』，同样留有余地，与『仍是完全的农业国』要强调的彻底性不符。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"completely agricultural 表『完完全全的农业国』，把工业化之前的状态推到极致，最能与后文工业社会形成强对照。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":7,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"however"},{"key":"B","text":"meanwhile"},{"key":"C","text":"therefore"},{"key":"D","text":"moreover"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"7.","reason":"第一段旧说 vs 第二段推翻 第一段整段陈述史学家的旧观点，第二段开头 This view, __(7)__, is generally thought to be wrong. 把这套观点判为错误。前后是『立旧说—破旧说』的对立，需要转折词。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"however 引出与前文相反的内容，正好把第一段的旧观点 Until recently most historians spoke very critically 与第二段『这观点是错的』衔接成转折，最契合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"meanwhile 表『与此同时』，用于并列同时发生之事，体现不出前后观点的对立。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"therefore 表『因此』，意味着第二段是第一段的结果；但第二段是推翻而非推论第一段，因果关系不成立。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"moreover 表『而且、更进一步』，用于同向叠加；而此处前后观点相反，方向不一致。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":8,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"at"},{"key":"B","text":"in"},{"key":"C","text":"about"},{"key":"D","text":"for"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"8.","reason":"specialists in+领域 Specialists __(8)__ history and economics，表『历史学和经济学领域的专家』。固定搭配为 specialist(s) in some field（某领域的专家），如 specialist in surgery。依据就在本句框架内。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"at 表『擅长』用于 be good at，但 specialist 后引领域不用 at，搭配错。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"specialist in 是固定搭配，意为『……领域的专家』，正好引出 history and economics 两个学科，最契合。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"about 表『关于』，specialist about 不是惯用搭配，无法表『某学科的专家』。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"for 表『为了/对于』，与 specialist 搭配引学科不地道，搭配错误。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":9,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"manifested"},{"key":"B","text":"approved"},{"key":"C","text":"shown"},{"key":"D","text":"speculated"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"9.","reason":"专家『证明』两个事实 Specialists __(8)__ history and economics have __(9)__ two things: that the period from 1650 to 1750 was __(10)__ by great poverty, and that industrialization certainly did not worsen and may have actually improved the conditions for the majority of the populace.，专家给出的是研究得出的、被当作定论的两件事，需要表『（用证据）表明、证实』的动词。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"manifest 指『（事物自身）显现、表露』，多用于症状、情绪显露，不用于『（人）通过研究证明某结论』。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"approve 是『批准、认可』，宾语应是计划、申请之类，不能带 that 从句表『证明事实』，语义不符。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"show 可作『（研究、证据）表明、证实』，后接 that 从句，正好表达专家研究证明了那两个结论，最契合。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"speculate 是『（无确据地）推测』，但此处两件事是专家确证的结论（用以推翻旧说），用推测会削弱其权威性，色彩冲突。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":10,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"noted"},{"key":"B","text":"impressed"},{"key":"C","text":"labeled"},{"key":"D","text":"marked"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"10.","reason":"be marked by=以……为特征 the period from 1650 to 1750 was __(10)__ by great poverty，要表达『1650-1750 这段时期以巨大贫困为特征』。be marked by 意为『以……为标志/特征』，正合此意，且与第一空所证结论（那段时期其实很穷）呼应。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"note 表『以……闻名』用 be noted for（如 noted for its beauty），不与 by 搭配表特征，搭配错。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"be impressed by 指『（人）对……印象深刻』，主语应是人，而此处主语是 period（时期），不能『被贫困打动』，语义不符。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"label 是『把……称作、贴标签』，后常接称呼（labeled a liar），表『被贫困贴标签』搭配与语义都不顺。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"be marked by 意为『以……为标志/特征』，the period was marked by great poverty 即『那段时期以巨大贫困为特征』，与专家证实的结论完全吻合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-1","kind":"reading","title":"Text 1","textNo":1,"directions":"Directions: Each of the passages below is followed by some questions. For each question there are four answers marked [A], [B], [C] and [D]. Read the passages carefully and choose the best answer to each of the questions. Then mark your answer on the ANSWER SHEET 1 by blackening the corresponding letter in the brackets. (40 points)","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 1","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-1","text":"Few creations of big technology capture the imagination like giant dams. Perhaps it is humankind's long suffering at the mercy of flood and drought that makes the idea of forcing the waters to do our bidding so fascinating. But to be fascinated is also, sometimes, to be blind. Several giant dam projects threaten to do more harm than good."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-2","text":"The lesson from dams is that big is not always beautiful. It doesn't help that building a big, powerful dam has become a symbol of achievement for nations and people striving to assert themselves. Egypt's leadership in the Arab world was cemented by the Aswan High Dam. Turkey's bid for First World status includes the giant Ataturk Dam."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-3","text":"But big dams tend not to work as intended. The Aswan Dam, for example, stopped the Nile flooding but deprived Egypt of the fertile silt that floods left—all in return for a giant reservoir of disease which is now so full of silt that it barely generates electricity."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-4","text":"And yet, the myth of controlling the waters persists. This week, in the heart of civilized Europe, Slovaks and Hungarians stopped just short of sending in the troops in their contention over a dam on the Danube. The huge complex will probably have all the usual problems of big dams. But Slovakia is bidding for independence from the Czechs, and now needs a dam to prove itself."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-5","text":"Meanwhile, in India, the World Bank has given the go-ahead to the even more wrong-headed Narmada Dam. And the bank has done this even though its advisors say the dam will cause hardship for the powerless and environmental destruction. The benefits are for the powerful, but they are far from guaranteed."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-6","text":"Proper, scientific study of the impacts of dams and of the cost and benefits of controlling water can help to resolve these conflicts. Hydroelectric power and flood control and irrigation are possible without building monster dams. But when you are dealing with myths, it is hard to be either proper, or scientific. It is time that the world learned the lessons of Aswan. You don't need a dam to be saved."}]},"questions":[{"n":11,"stem":"The third sentence of Paragraph 1 implies that ________.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"people would be happy if they shut their eyes to reality"},{"key":"B","text":"the blind could be happier than the sighted"},{"key":"C","text":"over-excited people tend to neglect vital things"},{"key":"D","text":"fascination makes people lose their eyesight"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"推断题","stemZh":"第一段第三句暗示________","choicesZh":{"A":"如果人们对现实视而不见,他们会感到快乐","B":"盲人可能比有视力的人更快乐","C":"过度兴奋的人往往会忽视重要的事情","D":"着迷使人丧失视力"},"analysis":{"type":"implies that 直接要求由原文的第三句推出一个未明说的含义，不是问字面意思。","parse":"题干 The third sentence of Paragraph 1 implies that ________. 是简单主谓宾结构：主语 The third sentence of Paragraph 1，谓语 implies，宾语是 that 引导的待补全名词性从句。结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"But to be fascinated is also, sometimes, to be blind.","locateZh":"但着迷有时也意味着盲目（视而不见）。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"shut their eyes to reality 是\"主动闭眼不看\"，且额外加了 would be happy——原文说的是\"着迷者无意识地失明\"，更没有任何句子说\"这样会让人开心\"。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"the blind could be happier than the sighted 把原文比喻意义上的 blind 当作生理上的盲人，再凭空加上\"比明眼人更快乐\"的比较；原文既无比较，也未涉及生理失明。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判说\"迷恋让人忽略真实危害\"，C 选项 over-excited people tend to neglect vital things 恰好把 fascinated 译为 over-excited、把 blind 译为 neglect vital things，是定位句的标准同义替换。","pairs":[{"orig":"to be fascinated","opt":"over-excited people"},{"orig":"to be blind","opt":"neglect vital things"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"fascination makes people lose their eyesight 用 makes... lose their eyesight 表示\"使人在生理上失去视力\"，把隐喻 blind 当成 lose eyesight 的同义改写——既偷换了语义层次，也加重了因果。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":12,"stem":"In Paragraph 5, \"the powerless\" probably refers to ________.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"areas short of electricity"},{"key":"B","text":"dams without power stations"},{"key":"C","text":"poor countries around India"},{"key":"D","text":"common people in the Narmada Dam area"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"在第五段中,\"the powerless\"可能指的是________","choicesZh":{"A":"缺电的地区","B":"没有发电站的水坝","C":"印度周边的贫穷国家","D":"Narmada大坝地区的普通民众"},"analysis":{"type":"\"the powerless\" probably refers to 直接问引号词具体指什么，是典型的词义/指代题。","parse":"题干 In Paragraph 5, \"the powerless\" probably refers to ________. 状语 In Paragraph 5 提前，主语 the powerless（引号词），谓语 probably refers to。probably 是程度副词缓和语气，不改变指代题本质。","locateEn":"And the bank has done this even though its advisors say the dam will cause hardship for the powerless and environmental destruction. The benefits are for the powerful, but they are far from guaranteed.","locateZh":"尽管世行的顾问们说这座大坝会给弱势者带来苦难、并造成环境破坏，世行还是放行了。受益方是有权有势者，但他们的收益也远非有保障。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"areas short of electricity 把 powerless 拆成 power（电）+ less（没有），译成\"缺电地区\"——但 P5 谈的是社会权力差异，而非电力短缺，且原文 hardship for the powerless 的语义场是\"受苦\"，不是\"缺电\"。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"dams without power stations 把 powerless 读成\"没有发电站的大坝\"——但题干 the powerless 是 the+adj 表一类\"人\"，不可能指\"物（大坝）\"，且原文从未提及\"无发电站的大坝\"。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"poor countries around India 把范围从 P5 明确的\"大坝建造区域的当地人\"扩大到\"印度周围的穷国\"，既扩大了主体（国家而非人），也扩大了地理范围（印度周边而非大坝区）。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判 powerless 是大坝所在地的普通人，common people in the Narmada Dam area 正是这个语义的完整落地——既给出\"普通人\"，又限定在 Narmada 大坝区域内，与 P5 完全契合。","pairs":[{"orig":"the powerless","opt":"common people"},{"orig":"Narmada Dam","opt":"in the Narmada Dam area"}]}}}}},{"n":13,"stem":"What is the myth concerning giant dams?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"They bring in more fertile soil."},{"key":"B","text":"They help defend the country."},{"key":"C","text":"They strengthen international ties."},{"key":"D","text":"They have universal control of the waters."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"关于巨型大坝的神话是什么?","choicesZh":{"A":"它们带来更肥沃的土壤","B":"它们有助于保卫国家","C":"它们加强国际联系","D":"它们对水域拥有普遍的控制权"},"analysis":{"type":"What is the myth concerning giant dams 是直接 wh- 提问，问一个被作者明确命名的概念的内容，是细节题。","parse":"题干 What is the myth concerning giant dams? 主系表结构，concerning giant dams 是后置定语限定 myth。concerning=about，是介词用法，考生若不熟悉容易误读为分词。","locateEn":"And yet, the myth of controlling the waters persists.","locateZh":"然而，控制水的神话仍在延续。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"They bring in more fertile soil. 把 P3 中 deprived Egypt of the fertile silt that floods left 的反例（大坝反而带走了肥沃淤泥）颠倒来用，且原文是\"洪水带来淤泥、大坝挡住淤泥\"，不是大坝带来淤泥。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"They help defend the country. 称大坝有助于国防——P2 谈的是大坝作为\"国际地位象征\"和\"国家凝聚力符号\"，从未出现 defend the country（军事防卫）的内涵。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"They strengthen international ties. 把 Egypt's leadership in the Arab world 与 Turkey's bid for First World status 误读为\"加强国际关系\"——但原文谈的是各国\"自我抬高地位\"，不是\"国家之间纽带变强\"，且 P4 多瑙河上的 Slovaks and Hungarians 恰恰因大坝几乎闹到 sending in the troops，国际关系反而更糟。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判 myth 的内容=控制水，选项 D They have universal control of the waters. 正是该内容的标准还原，其中 universal 来自作者多处暗示的\"全面驾驭水\"语调。","pairs":[{"orig":"controlling the waters","opt":"universal control of the waters"},{"orig":"forcing the waters to do our bidding","opt":"universal control of the waters"}]}}}}},{"n":14,"stem":"What the author tries to suggest may best be interpreted as ________.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"\"It's no use crying over spilt milk\""},{"key":"B","text":"\"More haste, less speed\""},{"key":"C","text":"\"Look before you leap\""},{"key":"D","text":"\"He who laughs last laughs best\""}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"作者试图表达的意思最好可以理解为________","choicesZh":{"A":"覆水难收","B":"欲速则不达","C":"三思而后行","D":"谁笑到最后,谁笑得最好"},"analysis":{"type":"What the author tries to suggest may best be interpreted as 直接问作者想传达的整体主张，且选项给的是四句英语谚语——典型的主旨升华题。","parse":"题干 What the author tries to suggest may best be interpreted as ________. 主语是名词性从句 What the author tries to suggest，谓语 may best be interpreted as，as 后接补语。may best 是情态动词 + 副词强调最高级\"最适合解读为\"。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"It's no use crying over spilt milk 意为\"覆水难收，不必懊悔\"——这是事后劝慰的语气；而作者通篇是\"事前警告\"：还来得及，别再建巨型大坝。立场上完全错位。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"More haste, less speed 意为\"欲速则不达\"，问题在\"快慢\"；但作者 Proper, scientific study 强调的是\"是否经过科学论证\"，问题在\"思考充分与否\"，不在做得太快。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判主旨=三思而后行，Look before you leap 字面=跳跃之前先看，对应 Proper, scientific study 与 to be fascinated is also, sometimes, to be blind 的双重警告，是与作者主张最贴合的格言。","pairs":[{"orig":"to be fascinated is also, sometimes, to be blind","opt":"Look before you leap"},{"orig":"Proper, scientific study of the impacts of dams","opt":"Look before you leap"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"He who laughs last laughs best 是\"笑到最后才笑得最好\"，强调最终胜出者；原文既无\"最终笑话谁\"的对比，也未谈\"耐心等到结局\"，与作者批判幻想、呼吁科学的主线无关。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-2","kind":"reading","title":"Text 2","textNo":2,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 2","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-1","text":"Well, no gain without pain, they say. But what about pain without gain? Everywhere you go in America, you hear tales of corporate revival. What is harder to establish is whether the productivity revolution that businessmen assume they are presiding over is for real."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-2","text":"The official statistics are mildly discouraging. They show that, if you lump manufacturing and services together, productivity has grown on average by 1.2% since 1987. That is somewhat faster than the average during the previous decade. And since 1991, productivity has increased by about 2% a year, which is more than twice the 1978-87 average. The trouble is that part of the recent acceleration is due to the usual rebound that occurs at this point in a business cycle, and so is not conclusive evidence of a revival in the underlying trend. There is, as Robert Rubin, the treasury secretary, says, a \"disjunction\" between the mass of business anecdote that points to a leap in productivity and the picture reflected by the statistics."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-3","text":"Some of this can be easily explained. New ways of organizing the workplace—all that re-engineering and downsizing—are only one contribution to the overall productivity of an economy, which is driven by many other factors such as joint investment in equipment and machinery, new technology, and investment in education and training. Moreover, most of the changes that companies make are intended to keep them profitable, and this need not always mean increasing productivity: switching to new markets or improving quality can matter just as much."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-4","text":"Two other explanations are more speculative. First, some of the business restructuring of recent years may have been ineptly done. Second, even if it was well done, it may have spread much less widely than people suppose."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-5","text":"Leonard Schlesinger, a Harvard academic and former chief executive of Au Bong Pain, a rapidly growing chain of bakery cafes, says that much \"re-engineering\" has been crude. In many cases, he believes, the loss of revenue has been greater than the reductions in cost. His colleague, Michael Beer, says that far too many companies have applied re-engineering in a mechanistic fashion, chopping out costs without giving sufficient thought to long-term profitability. BBDO's Al Rosenshine is blunter. He dismisses a lot of the work of re-engineering consultants as mere rubbish—\"the worst sort of ambulance chasing.\""}]},"questions":[{"n":15,"stem":"According to the author, the American economic situation is ________.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"not as good as it seems"},{"key":"B","text":"at its turning point"},{"key":"C","text":"much better than it seems"},{"key":"D","text":"near to complete recovery"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"态度题","stemZh":"根据作者的观点,美国的经济形势________。","choicesZh":{"A":"不如看起来的那么好","B":"处于转折点","C":"比看起来的要好得多","D":"接近完全复苏"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 According to the author, the American economic situation is 后接形容词性补语，索要的是作者对整体经济状况的总判断，而非某一段细节。","parse":"Q15 是补全式陈述句：主语 the American economic situation，系动词 is 后接空缺，四个选项分别填一种判断（比喻性或副词性短语），结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"A 项以「不如看上去那么好」精准对应作者全文的怀疑极性，且既覆盖首段的「表象」也覆盖二段的「数据」，是预判的同义替换。","pairs":[{"orig":"What is harder to establish is whether the productivity revolution that businessmen assume they are presiding over is for real.","opt":"not as good as it seems"},{"orig":"a \"disjunction\" between the mass of business anecdote that points to a leap in productivity and the picture reflected by the statistics","opt":"not as good as it seems"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"at its turning point 暗示经济正处在由坏转好或由好转坏的拐点，原文从未给出「拐点」信号——既无时间节点也无 turn ／ shift 之类极性反转语。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"much better than it seems 与作者整体怀疑立场极性相反；原文是「看上去好、实则未必」，选项却是「看上去不如实际好」，方向颠倒。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"near to complete recovery 要求文章给出「接近全面复苏」的证据，原文只提 tales of corporate revival 是流传的叙事，作者本人正在质疑这种叙事，远未承认「接近复苏」。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":16,"stem":"The official statistics on productivity growth ________.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"exclude the usual rebound in a business cycle"},{"key":"B","text":"fall short of businessmen's anticipation"},{"key":"C","text":"meet the expectation of business people"},{"key":"D","text":"fail to reflect the true state of economy"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"关于生产率增长的官方统计数据________。","choicesZh":{"A":"排除了商业周期中的常规反弹","B":"未达到商人的预期","C":"符合商界人士的预期","D":"未能反映经济的真实状况"},"analysis":{"type":"The official statistics on productivity growth 把对象锁死在官方统计这一具体客体，要的是关于它的客观判断，不涉及作者整体态度。","parse":"Q16 同为补全式陈述句：主语 The official statistics on productivity growth 由 on 短语后置修饰，系动词后接判断短语；结构清晰、无嵌套从句。","locateEn":"The official statistics are mildly discouraging. ... There is, as Robert Rubin, the treasury secretary, says, a \"disjunction\" between the mass of business anecdote that points to a leap in productivity and the picture reflected by the statistics.","locateZh":"官方统计稍稍令人失望。……正如财政部长鲁宾所言，关于「生产率大幅跃升」的大量商业坊间叙事，与统计数据所反映的真实图景之间，存在一道「裂缝」。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"exclude the usual rebound in a business cycle 把段中 the usual rebound that occurs at this point in a business cycle 偷换为「统计排除了这种反弹」。原文恰恰相反——统计是「包含」了这种反弹，作者借此提醒不能据此断言生产率革命。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判定为「统计低于商人感受」，B 项 fall short of businessmen's anticipation 与之逐词对应——主语都是统计，谓语都是「不及」，比较对象都是商人方。","pairs":[{"orig":"a \"disjunction\" between the mass of business anecdote that points to a leap in productivity and the picture reflected by the statistics","opt":"fall short of businessmen's anticipation"},{"orig":"mildly discouraging","opt":"fall short of businessmen's anticipation"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"meet the expectation of business people 与原文「商人感受到 leap，但统计只是 mildly discouraging」恰好相反；统计与商人预期相左而非吻合。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"fail to reflect the true state of economy 把「统计与商人叙事有落差」夸大为「统计未能反映经济真相」；原文只说两者之间存在 disjunction，并没有判定统计与商人哪一方才是「真相」，作者反而更倾向怀疑商人的叙事。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":17,"stem":"The author raises the question \"what about pain without gain?\" because ________.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"he questions the truth of \"no gain without pain\""},{"key":"B","text":"he does not think the productivity revolution works"},{"key":"C","text":"he wonders if the official statistics are misleading"},{"key":"D","text":"he has conclusive evidence for the revival of businesses"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"作者提出\"那么没有收益的痛苦呢?\"这个问题,是因为________。","choicesZh":{"A":"他质疑\"没有付出就没有收获\"的真实性","B":"他认为生产率革命没有起作用","C":"他怀疑官方统计数据是否具有误导性","D":"他有企业复苏的确凿证据"},"analysis":{"type":"The author raises the question \"what about pain without gain?\" because 直接问作者抛出这句反问的原因，正是例证目的题的句式。","parse":"Q17 主句 The author raises the question \"what about pain without gain?\"，宾语是引号内的反问句；后接 because 引导原因从句的待补位置；引号内容只是提问对象，不是逻辑主干。","locateEn":"Well, no gain without pain, they say. But what about pain without gain? Everywhere you go in America, you hear tales of corporate revival. What is harder to establish is whether the productivity revolution that businessmen assume they are presiding over is for real.","locateZh":"人们常说「不痛苦就没有收获」。可是只痛苦没有收获呢？走遍美国，到处都能听到企业复兴的故事。然而，更难以确证的是：商人们自以为正在引领的那场生产率革命，是否真的存在。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"he questions the truth of \"no gain without pain\" 把作者质疑的对象偷换为格言本身——原文并没有质疑 no gain without pain 的真伪，作者只是借这句格言反衬出「也可能 pain without gain」以质疑生产率革命。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判答案是「作者借反问表达对生产率革命真实性的怀疑」，B 项正是「作者不认为生产率革命奏效」，对应一致。","pairs":[{"orig":"What is harder to establish is whether the productivity revolution that businessmen assume they are presiding over is for real.","opt":"he does not think the productivity revolution works"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"he wonders if the official statistics are misleading 把作者质疑的对象从「生产率革命的真实性」偏移到「统计数据是否误导」。原文 P1 的反问紧接 productivity revolution ... is for real，是对革命本身的怀疑；统计是否误导是 P2 才展开的下游话题，且作者更倾向认为统计在揭示真相而非误导。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"he has conclusive evidence for the revival of businesses 与原文方向完全相反——so is not conclusive evidence of a revival in the underlying trend 明确说「并无确凿证据」，作者还在质疑而非掌握证据。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":18,"stem":"Which of the following statements is NOT mentioned in the passage?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Radical reforms are essential for the increase of productivity."},{"key":"B","text":"New ways of organizing workplaces may help to increase productivity."},{"key":"C","text":"The reduction of costs is not a sure way to gain long-term profitability."},{"key":"D","text":"The consultants are a bunch of good-for-nothings."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"以下哪项陈述在文中没有提及?","choicesZh":{"A":"彻底改革对于提高生产率至关重要。","B":"组织工作场所的新方式可能有助于提高生产率。","C":"降低成本并不是获得长期盈利能力的可靠途径。","D":"这些顾问是一群无用之人。"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following statements is NOT mentioned in the passage? 要求把每一项与原文一一比对，依据是文本是否出现，属于反向细节题。","parse":"Q18 是 wh-疑问句，主语 Which of the following statements，谓语为被动 is NOT mentioned，NOT 全大写是阅读时绝不可漏掉的反向信号。","locateEn":"New ways of organizing the workplace—all that re-engineering and downsizing—are only one contribution to the overall productivity of an economy, which is driven by many other factors such as joint investment in equipment and machinery, new technology, and investment in education and training. Moreover, most of the changes that companies make are intended to keep them profitable, and this need not always mean increasing productivity: switching to new markets or improving quality can matter just as much.","locateZh":"重新组织工作方式——所有那些再造工程和裁员——只是经济整体生产率的诸多贡献因素之一，后者还由设备机器的联合投资、新技术，以及对教育与培训的投资等众多因素驱动。此外，企业所做的大多数变革旨在维持盈利，这并不总意味着提高生产率：开拓新市场或改善质量同样重要。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"B／C／D 在 P3／P5 中均能逐一定位；A 项的关键词 essential ／ radical 在三段中都无对应，且与原文「再造只是因素之一」语义反向，因此为 NOT mentioned 的答案。","pairs":[{"orig":"New ways of organizing the workplace—all that re-engineering and downsizing—are only one contribution to the overall productivity of an economy, which is driven by many other factors such as joint investment in equipment and machinery, new technology, and investment in education and training.","opt":"Radical reforms are essential for the increase of productivity."}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"New ways of organizing workplaces may help to increase productivity. 与 New ways of organizing the workplace—all that re-engineering and downsizing—are only one contribution to the overall productivity of an economy 直接对应——原文承认新方式是生产率的贡献之一，相当于「可能有助于提高生产率」，故被文章提及，不选。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"The reduction of costs is not a sure way to gain long-term profitability. 同时对应 Moreover, most of the changes that companies make are intended to keep them profitable, and this need not always mean increasing productivity 与 chopping out costs without giving sufficient thought to long-term profitability——后者更直接指出削减成本未足以保障长期盈利。已被提及，不选。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"The consultants are a bunch of good-for-nothings. 对应 He dismisses a lot of the work of re-engineering consultants as mere rubbish——dismisses ... as mere rubbish 即「贬为废物」，与 good-for-nothings 等值。已被提及，不选。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-3","kind":"reading","title":"Text 3","textNo":3,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 3","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-1","text":"Science has long had an uneasy relationship with other aspects of culture. Think of Galileo's 17th-century trial for his rebelling belief before the Catholic Church or poet William Blake's harsh remarks against the mechanistic worldview of Isaac Newton. The schism between science and the humanities has, if anything, deepened in this century."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-2","text":"Until recently, the scientific community was so powerful that it could afford to ignore its critics—but no longer. As funding for science has declined, scientists have attacked \"anti-science\" in several books, notably Higher Superstition, by Paul R. Gross, a biologist at the University of Virginia, and Norman Levitt, a mathematician at Rutgers University; and The Demon-Haunted World, by Carl Sagan of Cornell University."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-3","text":"Defenders of science have also voiced their concerns at meetings such as \"The Flight from Science and Reason,\" held in New York City in 1995, and \"Science in the Age of (Mis) information,\" which assembled last June near Buffalo."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-4","text":"Anti-science clearly means different things to different people. Gross and Levitt find fault primarily with sociologists, philosophers and other academics who have questioned science's objectivity. Sagan is more concerned with those who believe in ghosts, creationism and other phenomena that contradict the scientific worldview."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-5","text":"A survey of news stories in 1996 reveals that the anti-science tag has been attached to many other groups as well, from authorities who advocated the elimination of the last remaining stocks of smallpox virus to Republicans who advocated decreased funding for basic research."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-6","text":"Few would dispute that the term applies to the Unabomber, whose manifesto, published in 1995, scorns science and longs for return to a pre-technological utopia. But surely that does not mean environmentalists concerned about uncontrolled industrial growth are anti-science, as an essay in US News & World Report last May seemed to suggest."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-7","text":"The environmentalists, inevitably, respond to such critics. The true enemies of science, argues Paul Ehrlich of Stanford University, a pioneer of environmental studies, are those who question the evidence supporting global warming, the depletion of the ozone layer and other consequences of industrial growth."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-8","text":"Indeed, some observers fear that the anti-science epithet is in danger of becoming meaningless. \"The term 'anti-science' can lump together too many, quite different things,\" notes Harvard University philosopher Gerald Holton in his 1993 work Science and Anti-Science. \"They have in common only one thing that they tend to annoy or threaten those who regard themselves as more enlightened.\""}]},"questions":[{"n":19,"stem":"The word \"schism\" (Line 4, Paragraph 1) in the context probably means ________.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"confrontation"},{"key":"B","text":"dissatisfaction"},{"key":"C","text":"separation"},{"key":"D","text":"contempt"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"文中\"schism\"一词(第一段第四行)在上下文中可能意为________。","choicesZh":{"A":"对抗","B":"不满","C":"分离","D":"轻蔑"},"analysis":{"type":"The word \"schism\" (Line 4, Paragraph 1) in the context probably means 是词义题的标准句式——给词、给坐标、问 in the context 的含义。","parse":"Q19 是个待补全的陈述句，主干 The word \"schism\" probably means ___；插入语 (Line 4, Paragraph 1) 给坐标，in the context 提醒考生要看上下文不能查字典义。结构平铺，无陷阱。","locateEn":"The schism between science and the humanities has, if anything, deepened in this century.","locateZh":"在本世纪，科学与人文之间的裂痕如果说有什么变化的话，是加深了。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"confrontation 意为正面对峙、直接冲突，需要主动方；但 The schism 描述的是一种长期存在的状态，不是当下的对抗行为；Galileo 和 Blake 是历史例证，文章并未说当代科学与人文在正面对峙。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"dissatisfaction 指不满，是某一方的情绪体验，不能放在 between X and Y 之间；原文是双方之间的关系，不是某一方对另一方的情绪。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"四个选项里只有 separation 能自然嵌入 between science and the humanities 的结构并保留分裂含义，符合预判。","pairs":[{"orig":"The schism between science and the humanities","opt":"separation"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"contempt 是轻蔑，方向性极强（X contempt for Y），但定位句没有谁轻视谁的指向；且 Blake 抨击牛顿是历史例证，正文核心是 between 两方的状态，不是单方的轻蔑。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":20,"stem":"Paragraphs 2 and 3 are written to ________.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"discuss the cause of the decline of science's power"},{"key":"B","text":"show the author's sympathy with scientists"},{"key":"C","text":"explain the way in which science develops"},{"key":"D","text":"exemplify the division of science and the humanities"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"第二段和第三段旨在________。","choicesZh":{"A":"讨论科学力量衰落的原因","B":"表达作者对科学家的同情","C":"解释科学发展的方式","D":"例证科学与人文学科的分离"},"analysis":{"type":"Paragraphs 2 and 3 are written to 在问两段被写出来是为了做什么——属于段落作用/例证目的题，要把这两段当作论据，找它支撑的论点。","parse":"Q20 主语 Paragraphs 2 and 3，被动语态 are written to ___ 接动词不定式补全，无陷阱。","locateEn":"Until recently, the scientific community was so powerful that it could afford to ignore its critics—but no longer. As funding for science has declined, scientists have attacked \"anti-science\" in several books...","locateZh":"直到不久前，科学界还强大到可以无视其批评者——但现在不行了。随着科学研究经费下降，科学家在多本书中抨击\"反科学\"……","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"discuss the cause of the decline of science's power 把 funding for science has declined 当成两段的中心，但这只是 P2 解释科学家为何反击的一个背景从句，不是 P2P3 在全文中的功能；P3 完全没涉及 science's power 的衰退原因。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"show the author's sympathy with scientists 假设作者偏袒科学家阵营，但 P2P3 是客观罗列书名/会议，没有任何 surely 这类作者情感词；后文 P7 环保人士反击同样被客观呈现，作者全程不站队。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"explain the way in which science develops 把段落主题偷换成科学发展方式，但 P2P3 讲的是科学界对外界批评的回应（出书、开会），不是科学自身怎样发展。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"其它选项要么只看 P2 表层（A、B），要么改换话题（C），只有 D 同时点明段落功能 exemplify 和被支撑论点 division of science and the humanities——这恰是 P1 schism deepened 的同义改写。","pairs":[{"orig":"The schism between science and the humanities has, if anything, deepened in this century","opt":"exemplify the division of science and the humanities"}]}}}}},{"n":21,"stem":"Which of the following is true according to the passage?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Environmentalists were blamed for anti-science in an essay."},{"key":"B","text":"Politicians are not subject to the labeling of anti-science."},{"key":"C","text":"The \"more enlightened\" tend to tag others as anti-science."},{"key":"D","text":"Tagging environmentalists as \"anti-science\" is justifiable."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据文章,下列哪项是正确的?","choicesZh":{"A":"环保主义者在一篇文章中被指责为反科学。","B":"政治家不受反科学标签的约束。","C":"更开明的人倾向于给其他人贴上反科学的标签。","D":"给环保主义者贴上\"反科学\"标签是正当的。"},"analysis":{"type":"true according to the passage 限定答案必须有原文依据，且四个选项分布在文章不同位置，需要逐项定位——这是典型细节判断题。","parse":"Q21 主语 Which of the following，谓语 is true，状语 according to the passage。结构平铺直叙，无陷阱；according to the passage 是硬约束——结论必须来自文本，不能凭常识。","locateEn":"But surely that does not mean environmentalists concerned about uncontrolled industrial growth are anti-science, as an essay in US News & World Report last May seemed to suggest.","locateZh":"但是，关注失控工业增长的环保人士肯定不能因此被算作反科学者——尽管去年五月《美国新闻与世界报道》的一篇文章似乎是这么暗示的。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"其它选项要么与 P5 P8 冲突（B、D），要么超出文本（C 见排除），只有 A 把 P6 这条原文事实直接复述，且不掺入作者立场。","pairs":[{"orig":"environmentalists concerned about uncontrolled industrial growth are anti-science, as an essay in US News & World Report last May seemed to suggest","opt":"Environmentalists were blamed for anti-science in an essay"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Politicians are not subject to the labeling of anti-science 与 Republicans who advocated decreased funding for basic research 直接矛盾——共和党人就是政客，他们已被贴上 anti-science 标签。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"The \"more enlightened\" tend to tag others as anti-science 把 P8 的描述（被 anti-science 标签骚扰到的人是\"more enlightened\"）反向改成\"more enlightened 主动给别人贴标签\"——原文只说他们觉得被冒犯，没说他们是贴标者。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Tagging environmentalists as \"anti-science\" is justifiable 是作者在 But surely that does not mean 中明确反对的论断；作者用 surely 强烈否定贴标合理性，选项却说是合理的。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":22,"stem":"The author's attitude toward the issue of \"science vs. anti-science\" is ________.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"impartial"},{"key":"B","text":"subjective"},{"key":"C","text":"biased"},{"key":"D","text":"puzzling"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"态度题","stemZh":"作者对\"科学与反科学\"问题的态度是________。","choicesZh":{"A":"公正的","B":"主观的","C":"有偏见的","D":"令人困惑的"},"analysis":{"type":"The author's attitude toward the issue ... is 是态度题的标准句式，问作者立场——属于第五步主旨/态度的特殊路径。","parse":"Q22 主干 The author's attitude is ___，待补形容词；介词短语 toward the issue of \"science vs. anti-science\" 限定态度的对象——是对整场争论的态度，不是对单方的支持。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"P1 至 P8 全程是新闻报道式呈现各方说法，作者唯一一次插话是反对乱贴标签，末段借专家口吻总结；这些证据收敛到 impartial 这一中立态度，与预判一致。","pairs":[{"orig":"The term 'anti-science' can lump together too many, quite different things","opt":"impartial"},{"orig":"But surely that does not mean environmentalists concerned about uncontrolled industrial growth are anti-science","opt":"impartial"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"subjective 指作者带强烈主观色彩，但全文 P2P3P4P5P7P8 都是引述他人观点、列举事实，没有第一人称评论或情感渲染；选项与文本基调相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"biased 指作者偏向某方，但作者唯一一次插话 surely that does not mean 是反对极化贴标签，没有偏向 science 或 anti-science 任何一方；选项无文本支撑。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"puzzling 指令人困惑，这是读者对文章的感受，不是作者本人的态度；况且文章脉络（P1 抛 schism → P2P3 例证 → P4-P7 各方定义 → P8 收尾）清晰，并不令人困惑。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-4","kind":"reading","title":"Text 4","textNo":4,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 4","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-1","text":"Emerging from the 1980 census is the picture of a nation developing more and more regional competition, as population growth in the Northeast and Midwest reaches a near standstill."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-2","text":"This development—and its strong implications for US politics and economy in years ahead—has enthroned the South as America's most densely populated region for the first time in the history of the nation's head counting."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-3","text":"Altogether, the US population rose in the 1970s by 23.2 million people—numerically the third-largest growth ever recorded in a single decade. Even so, that gain adds up to only 11.4 percent, lowest in American annual records except for the Depression years."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-4","text":"Americans have been migrating south and west in larger numbers since World War II, and the pattern still prevails."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-5","text":"Three sun-belt states—Florida, Texas and California—together had nearly 10 million more people in 1980 than a decade earlier. Among large cities, San Diego moved from 14th to 8th and San Antonio from 15th to 10th—with Cleveland and Washington, D.C., dropping out of the top 10."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-6","text":"Not all that shift can be attributed to the movement out of the snow belt, census officials say. Nonstop waves of immigrants played a role, too—and so did bigger crops of babies as yesterday's \"baby boom\" generation reached its child-bearing years."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-7","text":"Moreover, demographers see the continuing shift south and west as joined by a related but newer phenomenon: More and more, Americans apparently are looking not just for places with more jobs but with fewer people, too. Some instances:"},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-8","text":"■Regionally, the Rocky Mountain states reported the most rapid growth rate—37.1 percent since 1970 in a vast area with only 5 percent of the US population."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-9","text":"■Among states, Nevada and Arizona grew fastest of all: 63.5 and 53.1 percent respectively. Except for Florida and Texas, the top 10 in rate of growth is composed of Western states with 7.5 million people—about 9 per square mile."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-10","text":"The flight from overcrowdedness affects the migration from snow belt to more bearable climates."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-11","text":"Nowhere do 1980 census statistics dramatize more the American search for spacious living than in the Far West. There, California added 3.7 million to its population in the 1970s, more than any other state."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-12","text":"In that decade, however, large numbers also migrated from California, mostly to other parts of the West. Often they chose—and still are choosing—somewhat colder climates such as Oregon, Idaho and Alaska in order to escape smog, crime and other plagues of urbanization in the Golden State."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-13","text":"As a result, California's growth rate dropped during the 1970s, to 18.5 percent—little more than two thirds the 1960s' growth figure and considerably below that of other Western states."}]},"questions":[{"n":23,"stem":"Discerned from the perplexing picture of population growth the 1980 census provided, America in 1970s ________.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"enjoyed the lowest net growth of population in history"},{"key":"B","text":"witnessed a southwestern shift of population"},{"key":"C","text":"underwent an unparalleled period of population growth"},{"key":"D","text":"brought to a standstill its pattern of migration since World War II"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"从1980年人口普查提供的令人困惑的人口增长图景中可以看出,20世纪70年代的美国________。","choicesZh":{"A":"经历了历史上最低的人口净增长","B":"见证了人口向西南部转移","C":"经历了一个空前的人口增长时期","D":"使其自第二次世界大战以来的迁移模式陷入停滞"},"analysis":{"type":"America in 1970s ________ 是一个待补全的客观陈述句，没有 infer/imply/suggest，也不是问 main idea，要求选出与原文事实一致的描述。","parse":"Discerned from the perplexing picture of population growth the 1980 census provided, America in 1970s ________：句首是过去分词短语作状语，省略了被动主语；其中 population growth the 1980 census provided 是省略了关系词 that 的定语从句，修饰 picture。主干仅是 America in 1970s + 选项内容，结构上无陷阱。","locateEn":"Altogether, the US population rose in the 1970s by 23.2 million people—numerically the third-largest growth ever recorded in a single decade. Even so, that gain adds up to only 11.4 percent, lowest in American annual records except for the Depression years.","locateZh":"总的来看，1970 年代美国人口增长了 2320 万——就绝对数字而言，这是单个十年中有史以来第三大的增长。即便如此，这一增量也只折合 11.4%，是美国历年记录中除大萧条年代之外的最低值。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"enjoyed the lowest net growth of population in history 把原文的\"增长率最低\"换成了\"净增长最低\"，并去掉了\"除大萧条以外\"的限定。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判的\"南向位移\"与 southwestern shift of population 字面契合，且该项不涉及任何被原文否定的极端断言，故锁 B。","pairs":[{"orig":"enthroned the South as America's most densely populated region for the first time in the history of the nation's head counting","opt":"witnessed a southwestern shift of population"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"underwent an unparalleled period of population growth 说\"经历了空前的人口增长期\"，与定位句 lowest in American annual records except for the Depression years 直接相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"brought to a standstill its pattern of migration since World War II 称二战以来的迁移模式停滞，原文 Americans have been migrating south and west in larger numbers since World War II, and the pattern still prevails 明确说该模式仍在继续。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":24,"stem":"The census distinguished itself from previous studies on population movement in that ________.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"it stresses the climatic influence on population distribution"},{"key":"B","text":"it highlights the contribution of continuous waves of immigrants"},{"key":"C","text":"it reveals the Americans' new pursuit of spacious living"},{"key":"D","text":"it elaborates the delayed effects of yesterday's \"baby boom\""}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"这次人口普查与以往的人口流动研究的不同之处在于________。","choicesZh":{"A":"它强调气候对人口分布的影响","B":"它突出了持续移民浪潮的贡献","C":"它揭示了美国人对宽敞居住空间的新追求","D":"它详细阐述了昨日\"婴儿潮\"的延迟效应"},"analysis":{"type":"The census distinguished itself from previous studies on population movement in that ________ 是要求回原文找出一处具体差异的客观陈述题，不要求归纳全文。","parse":"The census distinguished itself from previous studies on population movement in that ________：主干是 The census distinguished itself from previous studies，介词短语 on population movement 修饰 studies；in that 是连词，意为\"在于；因为\"，引出宾语从句，从句的核心信息就是选项填入的内容。","locateEn":"Moreover, demographers see the continuing shift south and west as joined by a related but newer phenomenon: More and more, Americans apparently are looking not just for places with more jobs but with fewer people, too.","locateZh":"此外，人口学家观察到，伴随这种持续的南移与西移，还出现了一种相关但更新的现象：越来越多的美国人显然不仅在寻找工作机会更多的地方，也在寻找人更少的地方。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"it stresses the climatic influence on population distribution 把气候说成本普查的\"突出新发现\"，但原文 The flight from overcrowdedness affects the migration from snow belt to more bearable climates 把气候迁移定位为被\"逃离拥挤\"所影响的次要因素，并非新意所在。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"it highlights the contribution of continuous waves of immigrants 把\"移民\"视作普查的核心新意，但 Not all that shift can be attributed to the movement out of the snow belt, census officials say. Nonstop waves of immigrants played a role, too 把移民定位为众多原因之一（played a role, too），并未被强调为新意。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"四个选项中只有 C 命中\"宽敞居住\"这一被原文反复强调的新现象；其余三项都对应原文里被明确淡化的\"非主要新意\"。","pairs":[{"orig":"Americans apparently are looking not just for places with more jobs but with fewer people, too","opt":"it reveals the Americans' new pursuit of spacious living"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"it elaborates the delayed effects of yesterday's \"baby boom\" 把\"婴儿潮\"提升为重点，但原文 so did bigger crops of babies as yesterday's \"baby boom\" generation reached its child-bearing years 只一句带过，作为人口南移的补充原因之一，并非独特新意。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":25,"stem":"We can see from the available statistics that ________.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"California was once the most thinly populated area in the whole US"},{"key":"B","text":"the top 10 states in growth rate of population were all located in the West"},{"key":"C","text":"cities with better climates benefited unanimously from migration"},{"key":"D","text":"Arizona ranked second of all states in its growth rate of population"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"从现有统计数据可以看出________。","choicesZh":{"A":"California曾经是全美国人口最稀少的地区","B":"人口增长率排名前10位的州都位于西部","C":"气候条件更好的城市无一例外地受益于人口迁移","D":"Arizona在所有州中人口增长率排名第二"},"analysis":{"type":"We can see from the available statistics that ________ 是要求从客观数据出发判断各项陈述真伪，需要把四个选项各自回原文比对，是典型的数字细节题。","parse":"We can see from the available statistics that ________：主干 We can see that...，from the available statistics 是状语限定信息来源；that 后的宾语从句即选项内容。结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"Among states, Nevada and Arizona grew fastest of all: 63.5 and 53.1 percent respectively. Except for Florida and Texas, the top 10 in rate of growth is composed of Western states with 7.5 million people—about 9 per square mile.","locateZh":"在各州之中，内华达和亚利桑那增长最快：分别为 63.5% 和 53.1%。除了佛罗里达和得克萨斯外，增长率前十名的州都是西部州，共 750 万人口——约每平方英里 9 人。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"California was once the most thinly populated area in the whole US 称加州曾是全美人口最稀疏的地区，原文对加州的描述是 California added 3.7 million to its population in the 1970s, more than any other state 与 California's growth rate dropped during the 1970s, to 18.5 percent，从未提及\"最稀疏\"。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"the top 10 states in growth rate of population were all located in the West 说前十州\"全部\"位于西部，原文 Except for Florida and Texas, the top 10 in rate of growth is composed of Western states 明确把佛州、得州排除在西部之外。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"cities with better climates benefited unanimously from migration 称\"气候更好的城市无一例外都受益\"，但原文 Often they chose—and still are choosing—somewhat colder climates such as Oregon, Idaho and Alaska 显示人们也大量迁向较冷地区，气候并非唯一吸引项。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"D 把\"Arizona = 53.1% = 排名第二\"复述得字字落地；A、B、C 都和原文数字或限定不符。","pairs":[{"orig":"Nevada and Arizona grew fastest of all: 63.5 and 53.1 percent respectively","opt":"Arizona ranked second of all states in its growth rate of population"}]}}}}},{"n":26,"stem":"The word \"demographers\" (Line 1, Paragraph 8) most probably means ________.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"people in favor of the trend of democracy"},{"key":"B","text":"advocates of migration between states"},{"key":"C","text":"scientists engaged in the study of population"},{"key":"D","text":"conservatives clinging to old patterns of life"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"第8段第1行中\"demographers\"一词最可能的意思是________。","choicesZh":{"A":"支持民主趋势的人","B":"州际迁移的倡导者","C":"从事人口研究的科学家","D":"固守旧生活模式的保守派"},"analysis":{"type":"The word \"demographers\" (Line 1, Paragraph 8) most probably means ________ 显式给出待解词与位置，标准词义题模板。","parse":"The word \"demographers\" (Line 1, Paragraph 8) most probably means ________：主干 The word means...，most probably 是程度状语表\"很可能\"，提示答案是上下文最合理推断、而非绝对定义。","locateEn":"Moreover, demographers see the continuing shift south and west as joined by a related but newer phenomenon: More and more, Americans apparently are looking not just for places with more jobs but with fewer people, too.","locateZh":"此外，人口学家观察到，伴随这种持续的南移与西移，还出现了一种相关但更新的现象：越来越多的美国人显然不仅在寻找工作机会更多的地方，也在寻找人更少的地方。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"people in favor of the trend of democracy 利用考生对前缀 demo- 的直觉，把它联想为\"民主拥护者\"，但句中 demographers 的行为\"观察人口转移\"与民主无关。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"advocates of migration between states 用 \"migration between states\" 借住原文话题，把 demographers 从中性观察者偷换为\"主张州际迁移\"的倡导者；原文 see... as 表示客观观察，并无主张迁移之意。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"上下文功能（研究人口转移）+词根线索（demo-/-graph-）共同指向\"人口学家\"，C 项与之最贴。","pairs":[{"orig":"demographers see the continuing shift south and west as joined by a related but newer phenomenon","opt":"scientists engaged in the study of population"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"conservatives clinging to old patterns of life 称\"固守旧生活方式的保守派\"，与 demographers 在原文中作为客观观察者的角色无关，且原文整段在讲\"新现象\"，与 clinging to old patterns 反向。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-5","kind":"reading","title":"Text 5","textNo":5,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 5","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-5-1","text":"Scattered around the globe are more than 100 small regions of isolated volcanic activity known to geologists as hot spots. Unlike most of the world's volcanoes, they are not always found at the boundaries of the great drifting plates that make up the earth's surface; on the contrary, many of them lie deep in the interior of a plate. Most of the hot spots move only slowly, and in some cases the movement of the plates past them has left trails of dead volcanoes. The hot spots and their volcanic trails are milestones that mark the passage of the plates."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-5-2","text":"That the plates are moving is now beyond dispute. Africa and South America, for example, are moving away from each other as new material is injected into the sea floor between them. The complementary coastlines and certain geological features that seem to span the ocean are reminders of where the two continents were once joined. The relative motion of the plates carrying these continents has been constructed in detail, but the motion of one plate with respect to another cannot readily be translated into motion with respect to the earth's interior. It is not possible to determine whether both continents are moving in opposite directions or whether one continent is stationary and the other is drifting away from it. Hot spots, anchored in the deeper layers of the earth, provide the measuring instruments needed to resolve the question. From an analysis of the hot-spot population it appears that the African plate is stationary and that it has not moved during the past 30 million years."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-5-3","text":"The significance of hot spots is not confined to their role as a frame of reference. It now appears that they also have an important influence on the geophysical processes that propel the plates across the globe. When a continental plate comes to rest over a hot spot, the material rising from deeper layers creates a broad dome. As the dome grows, it develops deep fissures (cracks); in at least a few cases the continent may break entirely along some of these fissures, so that the hot spot initiates the formation of a new ocean. Thus just as earlier theories have explained the mobility of the continents, so hot spots may explain their mutability (inconstancy)."}]},"questions":[{"n":27,"stem":"The author believes that ________.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the motion of the plates corresponds to that of the earth's interior"},{"key":"B","text":"the geological theory about drifting plates has been proved to be true"},{"key":"C","text":"the hot spots and the plates move slowly in opposite directions"},{"key":"D","text":"the movement of hot spots proves the continents are moving apart"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"推断题","stemZh":"作者认为________。","choicesZh":{"A":"板块的运动与地球内部的运动相对应","B":"关于板块漂移的地质学理论已被证明是正确的","C":"热点与板块以相反方向缓慢移动","D":"热点的移动证明各大陆正在分离"},"analysis":{"type":"The author believes 没有具体对象，需要从作者的肯定性陈述中推断他对什么命题持确信态度。","parse":"The author believes 后接 that 引导的宾语从句留作空位，结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"That the plates are moving is now beyond dispute.","locateZh":"板块正在移动这一点现已毋庸置疑。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文明确说一块板块对另一块板块的相对运动\"无法轻易换算成相对地球内部的运动\"，A 项却说 motion of plates corresponds to that of the earth's interior，正好与原文相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"B 项把作者唯一明示的肯定立场\"板块漂移不再有争议\"完整复述为\"该理论已被证实\"，与预判完全吻合。","pairs":[{"orig":"That the plates are moving is now beyond dispute","opt":"the geological theory about drifting plates has been proved to be true"},{"orig":"the plates are moving","opt":"the geological theory about drifting plates"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说 hot spots \"move only slowly\"，并没有任何 hot spots 与 plates 相向而行的表述；\"opposite directions\" 是 C 项凭空添加的。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文是\"用 hot spots 作参照来判断大陆移动\"，而非\"hot spots 的移动证明大陆在分开\"；且作者的立场句强调的是板块漂移已被证实，而非用 hot spots 去证明。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":28,"stem":"That Africa and South America were once joined can be deduced from the fact that ________.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the two continents are still moving in opposite directions"},{"key":"B","text":"they have been found to share certain geological features"},{"key":"C","text":"the African plate has been stable for 30 million years"},{"key":"D","text":"over 100 hot spots are scattered all around the globe"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"推断题","stemZh":"非洲和南美洲曾经连接在一起,这可以从________这一事实推断出来。","choicesZh":{"A":"这两个大陆仍在朝相反方向移动","B":"已发现它们具有某些共同的地质特征","C":"非洲板块已经稳定了3000万年","D":"全球各处分布着100多个热点"},"analysis":{"type":"can be deduced from the fact that 表明结论已经给出，问的是支撑结论的事实证据，是一种反向推断。","parse":"主干 \"That ... can be deduced from the fact that ___\"，That 引导的主语从句陈述事实，本题型常见，无理解陷阱。","locateEn":"The complementary coastlines and certain geological features that seem to span the ocean are reminders of where the two continents were once joined.","locateZh":"互补的海岸线与某些似乎横跨大洋的地质特征，提醒着人们两个大陆曾在哪里相连。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"两大洲现在 \"are moving away from each other\" 是板块漂移的体现，但这是\"现状证明运动\"，并非\"过去相连\"的直接事实证据；况且选项还加上 still 强调持续，与题干 once joined 的时间维度不匹配。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"B 项完整对应了原文 \"complementary coastlines and certain geological features that seem to span the ocean\" 这一事实证据，与预判中的\"互补海岸线 + 跨洋地质特征\"完全契合。","pairs":[{"orig":"certain geological features that seem to span the ocean","opt":"they have been found to share certain geological features"},{"orig":"The complementary coastlines","opt":"they have been found to share certain geological features"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"C 项陈述的是非洲板块过去 3000 万年静止，这是用 hot spots 作参照得出的结论，与\"两大洲曾相连\"没有直接因果关系。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"D 项的 100 多个 hot spots 来自首段对 hot spots 的定义，与\"非洲与南美洲曾相连\"是两件事，原文从未把数量当作两洲相连的证据。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":29,"stem":"The hot spot theory may prove useful in explaining ________.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the structure of the African plates"},{"key":"B","text":"the revival of dead volcanoes"},{"key":"C","text":"the mobility of the continents"},{"key":"D","text":"the formation of new oceans"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"热点理论可能有助于解释________。","choicesZh":{"A":"非洲板块的结构","B":"死火山的复活","C":"大陆的移动性","D":"新海洋的形成"},"analysis":{"type":"may prove useful in explaining 问 hot spot theory 能解释什么，答案是原文中作者明确写出的对象，属于具体信息细节。","parse":"主干 \"The hot spot theory may prove useful in explaining ___\"，prove 在此为系动词\"被证明是\"，并非\"证明\"的及物义，需防 A2 熟词僻义。","locateEn":"in at least a few cases the continent may break entirely along some of these fissures, so that the hot spot initiates the formation of a new ocean.","locateZh":"至少在少数情况下，大陆可能沿着这些裂缝完全裂开，于是 hot spot 启动了一个新海洋的形成。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文用 hot spots 推断出非洲板块静止，是把非洲板块当作被测量的对象，而非用 hot spot 理论解释\"非洲板块的结构\"；structure 在原文从未被作为话题。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说板块运动留下了 trails of dead volcanoes（死火山轨迹），并未谈\"死火山复活\"，更未说 hot spot 理论解释 revival；revival 本身就是原文从未出现的概念。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文末句 just as earlier theories have explained the mobility of the continents, so hot spots may explain their mutability 用 just as ... so ... 句式明确：mobility 是\"先前理论\"已经解释的对象，而 hot spots 解释的是 mutability；C 项把先前理论的功劳算到 hot spot 理论上。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"题干结构 \"useful in explaining X\" 中的 X 与原文 \"hot spot initiates X\" 中的 X 在结构上完全对位，D 项的 X 与原文宾语逐字对应。","pairs":[{"orig":"the hot spot initiates the formation of a new ocean","opt":"the formation of new oceans"}]}}}}},{"n":30,"stem":"The passage is mainly about ________.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the features of volcanic activities"},{"key":"B","text":"the importance of the theory about drifting plates"},{"key":"C","text":"the significance of hot spots in geophysical studies"},{"key":"D","text":"the process of the formation of volcanoes"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"这篇文章主要讨论________。","choicesZh":{"A":"火山活动的特征","B":"板块漂移理论的重要性","C":"热点在地球物理研究中的意义","D":"火山的形成过程"},"analysis":{"type":"The passage is mainly about 显式询问文章主旨，无需任何细节锚点。","parse":"\"is mainly about\" 是判定结构，简洁明确，无语法陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"全文只有第一段提到 volcanic activity，且只作为引出 hot spots 的背景；火山活动的特征本身从未被系统讨论。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"板块漂移理论虽在第二段被肯定，但全文并未围绕\"漂移板块理论的重要性\"展开论述，而是借这一理论引出 hot spots 的角色。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"C 项的 significance 与 hot spots 复用原文主词，再以 geophysical studies 上位概括地球物理诸议题，正好覆盖全文三段。","pairs":[{"orig":"The significance of hot spots is not confined to their role as a frame of reference","opt":"the significance of hot spots in geophysical studies"},{"orig":"Hot spots, anchored in the deeper layers of the earth, provide the measuring instruments needed to resolve the question","opt":"the significance of hot spots in geophysical studies"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文谈的是 hot spots 留下死火山轨迹和大陆裂开形成新海洋，从未描述\"火山如何形成\"的过程；formation of volcanoes 本身不是全文话题。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-b","kind":"translation","title":"Section II Part C 英译汉","directions":"Directions: Read the following passage carefully and then translate the underlined sentences into Chinese. Your translation must be written clearly on the ANSWER SHEET 2 . (15 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-b-1","text":"They were, by far, the largest and most distant objects that scientists had ever detected: a strip of enormous cosmic clouds some 15 billion light-years from earth. (31) But even more important, it was the farthest that scientists had been able to look into the past, for what they were seeing were the patterns and structures that existed 15 billion years ago. That was just about the moment that the universe was born. What the researchers found was at once both amazing and expected: the US National Aeronautics and Space Administration's Cosmic Background Explorer satellite—Cobe—had discovered landmark evidence that the universe did in fact begin with the primeval explosion that has become known as the Big Bang (the theory that the universe originated in an explosion from a single mass of energy)."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-2","text":"(32) The existence of the giant clouds was virtually required for the Big Bang, first put forward in the 1920s, to maintain its reign as the dominant explanation of the cosmos. According to the theory, the universe burst into being as a submicroscopic, unimaginably dense knot of pure energy that flew outward in all directions, emitting radiation as it went, condensing into particles and then into atoms of gas. Over billions of years, the gas was compressed by gravity into galaxies, stars, planets and eventually, even humans."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-3","text":"Cobe is designed to see just the biggest structures, but astronomers would like to see much smaller hot spots as well, the seeds of local objects like clusters and superclusters of galaxies. They shouldn't have long to wait. (33) Astrophysicists working with ground-based detectors at the South Pole and balloon-borne instruments are closing in on such structures, and may report their findings soon."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-4","text":"(34) If the small hot spots look as expected, that will be a triumph for yet another scientific idea, a refinement of the Big Bang called the inflationary universe theory. Inflation says that very early on, the universe expanded in size by more than a trillion trillion trillion trillion fold in much less than a second, propelled by a sort of antigravity. (35) Odd though it sounds, cosmic inflation is a scientifically plausible consequence of some respected ideas in elementary particle physics, and many astrophysicists have been convinced for the better part of a decade that it is true."}]},"sentences":[{"n":31,"en":"But even more important, it was the farthest that scientists had been able to look into the past, for what they were seeing were the patterns and structures that existed 15 billion years ago.","refZh":"但更为重要的是，这是科学家们所能回望到的最遥远的过去，因为他们当时看到的，正是存在于 150 亿年前的（宇宙）形态与结构。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"But even more important,","lit":"但更为重要的是，","role":"（句首插入语（评注状语））","note":"难点： important 后省略了 is，是评注性插入语 even more important 是 (what is) even more important 的省略，独立于主句之外，对全句作评价，译成「但更为重要的是」放句首即可，别硬塞进主干。"},{"en":"it was the farthest that scientists had been able to look into the past,","lit":"这是科学家们能够回望过去最为遥远的（一次）","role":"（主干（强调结构 it was…that…））","note":"难点： it was the farthest that… 是强调结构，look into the past=回望过去 这里 it was…that… 把 the farthest（最远）强调出来；the farthest 不是指距离最远的物体，而是接后面 look into the past，指「向过去回望得最远」。look into the past 直译「看进过去」不通，要具体化为「回溯 / 回望过去（的历史）」。"},{"en":"for what they were seeing were the patterns and structures","lit":"因为他们所看到的是（一些）图案和结构","role":"（原因状语从句（for 引导）+ 主语从句作主语）","note":"难点： for=因为（连词），what they were seeing 是主语从句 for 在这里是并列连词「因为」，引出原因，不是介词。what they were seeing（他们当时看到的东西）整体作从句主语，谓语是后一个 were。patterns and structures 译「图案（形态）和结构」。"},{"en":"that existed 15 billion years ago.","lit":"存在于 150 亿年前的","role":"（that 引导的定语从句（修饰 patterns and structures））","note":"难点： 15 billion=150 亿，定语从句修饰前面的名词 英文 billion=10 亿，15 billion=150 亿，是常考数字陷阱，别误译成「15 亿」。that existed… 是后置定语，修饰 the patterns and structures，调序时前移。"}]},{"n":32,"en":"The existence of the giant clouds was virtually required for the Big Bang, first put forward in the 1920s, to maintain its reign as the dominant explanation of the cosmos.","refZh":"巨型宇宙云团的存在，对于这一最早在 20 世纪 20 年代提出的大爆炸理论而言，实际上是其维持作为宇宙主导解释这一地位所必不可少的。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"The existence of the giant clouds was virtually required","lit":"这些巨大云团的存在实际上是被需要的","role":"（主干（主谓，被动语态））","note":"难点： the giant clouds 回指宇宙云带；was required 被动需转译 the giant clouds 指第 1 段那条「巨型宇宙云带」（见指代还原表）。was virtually required 直译「被实际地需要」很生硬，应转主动或意译为「实际上是必不可少的 / 是必需的」。virtually=实际上、几乎，不是「虚拟地」（熟词僻义易错）。"},{"en":"for the Big Bang,","lit":"对于大爆炸理论来说 / 大爆炸理论（要…）","role":"（for 引出逻辑主语（接后面的不定式））","note":"难点： for the Big Bang…to maintain 是「for + 名词 + 不定式」结构 这里 for 不是「为了」那么简单，它和后面的 to maintain its reign 构成「for sb./sth. to do」结构，the Big Bang 是不定式 to maintain 的逻辑主语，意思是「要让大爆炸理论维持其地位」。"},{"en":"first put forward in the 1920s,","lit":"（它）最早于 20 世纪 20 年代提出","role":"（过去分词短语作插入定语（修饰 the Big Bang））","note":"难点： put forward=提出；in the 1920s=20 世纪 20 年代 first put forward in the 1920s 是插入语，补充说明 the Big Bang 的来历，翻译时单独处理成「这一最早于 20 世纪 20 年代提出的理论」或加括号补出。put forward 是固定搭配「提出」。"},{"en":"to maintain its reign as the dominant explanation of the cosmos.","lit":"来维持它作为宇宙主导解释的统治地位","role":"（不定式短语作目的状语）","note":"难点： maintain its reign=维持其统治地位；dominant explanation=主导性解释 reign 本义「统治、王权」，此处比喻「（理论的）主导地位」，译「维持其统治地位 / 主导地位」；its 回指 the Big Bang。the cosmos=宇宙（=the universe 的同义替换）。"}]},{"n":33,"en":"Astrophysicists working with ground-based detectors at the South Pole and balloon-borne instruments are closing in on such structures, and may report their findings soon.","refZh":"利用南极的地基探测器和气球搭载仪器开展研究的天体物理学家们，正在逐步逼近这类（更小的）结构，并可能很快报告他们的研究发现。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Astrophysicists","lit":"天体物理学家们","role":"（主语）","note":"难点： astrophysicists=天体物理学家 astro-（天体）+ physicists（物理学家）= 天体物理学家，构词法可拆解，即便生词也能猜个八九不离十。"},{"en":"working with ground-based detectors at the South Pole and balloon-borne instruments","lit":"（正）使用着南极的地基探测器和气球搭载仪器的","role":"（现在分词短语作后置定语（修饰 Astrophysicists））","note":"难点： ground-based=地基的；balloon-borne=气球搭载的；working with 修饰前面的人 working with… 是后置定语修饰 Astrophysicists，不是谓语（谓语是后面的 are closing in）。ground-based detectors=设在地面的探测器（地基探测器），balloon-borne instruments=由气球搭载升空的仪器；-based、-borne 都是「以…为载体的」复合形容词。"},{"en":"are closing in on such structures,","lit":"正在逼近这类结构","role":"（主干谓语）","note":"难点： close in on=逐渐逼近/接近；such structures 回指更小的热斑 close in on 是固定短语「（逐渐）逼近、接近」，不能拆成「关闭」。such structures 回指上文 much smaller hot spots（见指代还原表），译时还原为「这类（更小的）结构」。"},{"en":"and may report their findings soon.","lit":"并且可能很快报告他们的发现","role":"（并列谓语）","note":"难点： findings=研究发现/成果（熟词僻义） findings 不是「找到的东西」泛指，在科研语境里专指「研究发现、研究成果」。and 连接的是与 are closing in 并列的另一个谓语 may report。"}]},{"n":34,"en":"If the small hot spots look as expected, that will be a triumph for yet another scientific idea, a refinement of the Big Bang called the inflationary universe theory.","refZh":"如果这些小型热斑的情形果真如人们预期的那样，那么这将是又一个科学构想的胜利——即对大爆炸理论的一种改进，也就是所谓的暴胀宇宙论。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"If the small hot spots look as expected,","lit":"如果这些小热斑看上去如所预期的那样","role":"（条件状语从句（if 引导））","note":"难点： as expected=正如预期；hot spots=热斑 look as expected 即 look as (they are) expected (to look)，省略结构，意为「（其样子）符合预期」。the small hot spots 指上文 much smaller hot spots，译「小（型）热斑」。"},{"en":"that will be a triumph for yet another scientific idea,","lit":"那将是又一个科学构想的胜利","role":"（主句）","note":"难点： triumph=巨大成功/胜利；yet another=又一个 triumph 译「重大胜利 / 成功」；yet another 强调「在已有理论之外、再添一个」，译「又一个、另一个」。that 指代前面「小热斑符合预期」这件事。"},{"en":"a refinement of the Big Bang","lit":"（即）大爆炸理论的一种精进/改良","role":"（同位语（解释 yet another scientific idea））","note":"难点： refinement=改进、精细化（抽象名词具体化） refinement 是抽象名词，直译「精炼」不达意；在「a refinement of the Big Bang」里指对大爆炸理论的「改进版、精修 / 完善」。这是 yet another scientific idea 的同位语，对它作解释。"},{"en":"called the inflationary universe theory.","lit":"被称为暴胀宇宙论的","role":"（过去分词短语作定语（修饰 a refinement））","note":"难点： the inflationary universe theory=暴胀宇宙论 called… 是后置定语，inflationary（膨胀的、暴胀的）来自 inflation（膨胀），此处是天文术语「暴胀宇宙论 / 膨胀宇宙说」，译时与第 35 句的 cosmic inflation 保持术语统一。"}]},{"n":35,"en":"Odd though it sounds, cosmic inflation is a scientifically plausible consequence of some respected ideas in elementary particle physics, and many astrophysicists have been convinced for the better part of a decade that it is true.","refZh":"尽管这听起来有些奇怪，但宇宙暴胀（理论）在科学上是站得住脚的，它是基本粒子物理学中一些公认观点的合理推论；而且近十年来的大部分时间里，许多天体物理学家一直确信它（宇宙暴胀）是真实存在的。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Odd though it sounds,","lit":"尽管这听起来很奇怪","role":"（让步状语从句（倒装 though））","note":"难点： Odd though it sounds=though it sounds odd（倒装让步） 这是「形容词 + though + 主谓」的倒装让步结构，等于 though it sounds odd，意为「尽管它听起来很奇怪」。it 指后面的 cosmic inflation。see odd（奇怪的）被提到句首是为让步语气，别被语序绕晕。"},{"en":"cosmic inflation is a scientifically plausible consequence of some respected ideas in elementary particle physics,","lit":"宇宙暴胀是基本粒子物理学中一些受人尊重的观点的一个科学上站得住脚的结果","role":"（主句（主系表））","note":"难点： plausible=（看似）合理可信的；consequence=推论/结果；elementary particle physics=基本粒子物理学 plausible 译「（科学上）讲得通的、合理可信的」；consequence 此处非「后果」，而是逻辑上的「推论、结果」；respected ideas 译「受到认可 / 公认的观点」；elementary particle physics 是术语「基本粒子物理学」（elementary 取「基本的」而非「初级的」）。"},{"en":"and many astrophysicists have been convinced for the better part of a decade","lit":"而且许多天体物理学家在近十年的大部分时间里一直确信","role":"（并列分句（and 引导））","note":"难点： the better part of a decade=十年里的大半时间；be convinced=确信 the better part of a decade 是固定表达「一个十年的大半 / 大部分时间」，即「七八年、近十年」，不是「十年中较好的部分」（字面陷阱）。have been convinced 现在完成时 +be convinced「一直深信」。"},{"en":"that it is true.","lit":"它是真实的","role":"（宾语从句（convinced 的内容））","note":"难点： it=cosmic inflation（回指主语） that it is true 中 it 回指本句主语 cosmic inflation（见指代还原表），还原后译「确信它（宇宙暴胀）是真实的 / 确有其事」，别让代词悬空。"}]}]},{"id":"section3","kind":"writing","title":"Section III 写作","directions":"36. Directions: [A] Study the following cartoon carefully and write an essay in no less than 150 words. [B] Your essay must be written clearly on the ANSWER SHEET 2. (15 points) [C] Your essay should meet the requirements below: 1. Write out the messages conveyed by the cartoon. 2. Give your commentsn.","prompt":"36. Directions: [A] Study the following cartoon carefully and write an essay in no less than 150 words. [B] Your essay must be written clearly on the ANSWER SHEET 2. (15 points) [C] Your essay should meet the requirements below: 1. Write out the messages conveyed by the cartoon. 2. Give your commentsn.","points":15,"image":{"src":"assets/writing/1998-section3.jpg","alt":"这是一幅漫画，漫画标题是一首打油诗： 如此承诺 各行各业兴承诺 欢迎监督不推脱 原本皆为分内事 何须高唱“文明歌” 漫画中有一只母鸡站在鸡窝中，母鸡身后有2…","width":"1172","height":"708","local":"assets/writing/1998-section3.jpg"},"model":{"essay":"As is vividly depicted in the cartoon, a hen stands proudly in its nest, holding a written pledge that solemnly promises its eggs will have no sharp corners and will surely contain a shell, egg white and yolk. Behind it lie two perfectly ordinary eggs. The humor is obvious: the hen is boasting about something that is simply what every hen naturally does. Simple as the drawing is, it conveys a thought-provoking message about the empty formalism prevailing in some trades today. Just as laying a normal egg is a hen's inborn duty, offering honest and qualified service is the basic obligation of any profession. Yet some restaurants, hospitals or shops proudly hang up grand slogans, welcoming supervision and vowing to serve civilly, as if fulfilling their plain responsibility deserved loud applause. Such showy commitments cost nothing and prove nothing; they merely turn duty into a performance and mislead the public with hollow words. Accordingly, we should value substance far above form. Instead of shouting fine-sounding slogans, individuals and organizations ought to quietly do what they are supposed to do and let real deeds speak. Only when everyone treats duty as duty, rather than as a favor worth advertising, can genuine trust and progress be built in our society.","translation":"如漫画生动描绘的那样，一只母鸡神气地站在鸡窝里，手举一份承诺书，郑重承诺自己下的蛋没有尖锐的棱角、并且保证有蛋皮、蛋清和蛋黄。它身后正躺着两个再普通不过的蛋。笑点显而易见：母鸡在为一件每只母鸡天生都会做的事大肆炫耀。\n画面虽简单，却传递出一个发人深省的信息——当今某些行业盛行的空洞形式主义。正如下一个正常的蛋是母鸡与生俱来的本分，提供诚实、合格的服务也是任何行业的基本义务。然而，一些餐馆、医院或商店却大张旗鼓地挂出标语，欢迎监督、承诺文明服务，仿佛履行分内之责就值得大加喝彩。这类花哨的承诺不费分文、也证明不了什么，只是把本职变成了表演，并用空话误导公众。\n因此，我们应当把实质看得远比形式重要。与其高喊动听的口号，个人与机构更应默默做好自己该做的事，让实实在在的行动说话。唯有当人人把分内事当作分内事、而非当成值得张扬的恩惠时，我们的社会才能建立起真正的信任与进步。","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"描述＋一句点寓意","text":"【第 1 段】 描述＋一句点寓意 。本段落实『先描画面，再点寓意』：前两句用一般现在时 stands/holding/promises 客观描述母鸡举承诺书、身后两蛋，只写与寓意相关的核心元素；末句 The humor is obvious 一句点破『为天生分内事邀功』，完成 Write out the messages conveyed by the cartoon 的任务，并为评论过渡。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"类比＋举例＋评价","text":"【第 2 段】 类比＋举例＋评价 。本段落实『类比＋举例撑起论证』：Just as… 把母鸡下蛋类比为各行业本职；Yet some restaurants, hospitals or shops… 举现实例子对应 欢迎监督不推脱；Such showy commitments cost nothing and prove nothing 一句给出评价，指出重形式轻实质之害，让评论有据。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"重申态度＋升华","text":"【第 3 段】 重申态度＋升华 。本段落实『重申态度＋给出建议』：Accordingly, we should value substance far above form 重申立场；Instead of… ought to… 给出具体建议；Only when… can… be built 升华到社会信任与进步，呼应打油诗 原本皆为分内事 的主旨，完成 Give your comments。"}],"wordCount":209}}],"questionCount":30,"objectiveCount":30,"answerTable":{"ans-section1":"完形填空（四选一） Section I （1–10 题） 1 A admitted · 2 B average · 3 D immediate · 4 A bulk · 5 D By · 6 D completely · 7 A however · 8 B in · 9 C shown · 10 D marked \n（逐题解析见 完形填空（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-1":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (1) （11–14 题） 11 C · 12 D · 13 D · 14 C \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-2":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (2) （15–18 题） 15 A · 16 B · 17 B · 18 A \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-3":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (3) （19–22 题） 19 C · 20 D · 21 A · 22 A \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-4":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (4) （23–26 题） 23 B · 24 C · 25 D · 26 C \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-5":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (5) （27–30 题） 27 B · 28 B · 29 D · 30 C \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-b":"英译汉（划线句子翻译） Section II Part B \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 英译汉（划线句子翻译）解析页","ans-section3":"写作 Section III \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页"},"coverage":{"objective":30,"explained":30,"missingSections":[]}};
